title: bob_first_meet
tags:
position: 0,0
---
<<set $bob_met = true>>
Bob: Heyup. Mind the lintel — old beam, older head.
Bob: Bob. I run the Inn, what's left of it. You'll be the one tuning the domes, I take it?
Bob: News travels, even out here. The mud carries it. Slowly.
-> Player: "How long has the Inn stood?"
    Bob: Longer than the maps say. The frame's Tartarian. I just patched the roof.
    Bob: Wood remembers. Walls remember. I try not to ask them what.
-> Player: "Can I rest here?"
    Bob: Aye, when the work's done. Restore the village and the bed's yours.
    Bob: A night's rest moves the world a moon onward. Earn it first.
-> Player: "Have you seen the others?"
    Bob: Milo comes through for stew. Lirael hums by the well. Anastasia I've only heard about.
    Bob: Cassian buys candles by the dozen, never explains why. Make of that what you will.
===

title: bob_inn_about
tags:
---
Bob: This Inn's been here through three floods and two silences.
Bob: The kettle's older than my grandfather and it still sings on cue.
Bob: People come, people go. The fire stays. That's the trade.
===

title: bob_rest_ready
tags:
---
Bob: Work's done, by the look of you. Dust on the boots, hum in the bones.
Bob: Bed's upstairs, second door. Sleep deep — the moon turns while you do.
Bob: When you wake, it won't be this moon anymore. That's how rest works, out here.
===

title: bob_warning_17th_hour
tags:
---
Bob: You feel it too, then. Around the seventeenth hour. The Inn creaks differently.
Bob: I keep the lamps trimmed those nights. Bad time for shadows to find an unfilled wick.
Bob: Tell Lirael, if you see her. She'll know what to do. She always does.
===

title: bob_lore_tartarians
tags:
---
Bob: I don't claim to know what the old folk built or why.
Bob: But I'll tell you this — the cellar floor's a single slab of stone, and it hums when the kettle hits the right note.
Bob: I don't go down there much. Cellar can keep its secrets.
===

title: bob_ambient_1
tags:
---
Bob: Stew's on. Always is. Don't ask what's in it.
===

title: bob_ambient_2
tags:
---
Bob: The wind's off the east tonight. Always brings stories the lamps don't like.
===

title: bob_farewell
tags:
---
Bob: Mind how you go. The mud's been quiet, which means it's listening.
Bob: Fire'll be lit when you're back. Always is.
===
